-- title:
--   Residue degree bound ≤ ψ(M') at height-one primes of X₀(M')
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K_0$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated by all quotients $f/g$ of $q$-expansions of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(M')$ having integral $q$-expansions, with $g$'s expansion nonzero. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $q$ and is generated by $\varpi$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K_0$ compatible with $A \to L \to K_0$. Let $j_0 \in K_0$ be nonzero with Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the } q\text{-expansion numerator of } j)$ under the coefficient embedding. Put $B_0 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), the subalgebra of elements of $K_0$ integral over $A[j_0]$, regarded as a $\mathrm{Polynomial}\,A$-algebra via the map sending $p$ to $p(j_0)$. Let $\mathfrak{Q} \subseteq B_0$ be a prime of height $1$ containing the image of $\varpi$, and let $\mathfrak{q} = \mathfrak{Q} \cap \mathrm{Polynomial}\,A$ be its contraction, with the localisation of $B_0$ at $\mathfrak{Q}$ an algebra over the localisation at $\mathfrak{q}$ lying over it. Then $\kappa(\mathfrak{Q})$ is a finite $\kappa(\mathfrak{q})$-module and $[\kappa(\mathfrak{Q}) : \kappa(\mathfrak{q})] \le \psi(M') = \sum_{d \mid M',\ d \text{ squarefree}} M'/d$.
--
--   This bounds the residue degree at a vertical height-one prime of the integral model $B_0$ of the modular curve $X_0(M')$ over $A[j]$ by the generic degree $[\,K_0 : L(j_0)\,] \le [\Gamma(1) : \Gamma_0(M')] = \psi(M')$. It feeds the separability statement for residue fields of this model at height-one primes above $\varpi$, where the matching lower bound turns the inequality into an identification of $\kappa(\mathfrak{Q})$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finite_and_finrank_residueField_le_dedekindPsi_polynomial_chartAlgFin_gamma0_of_height_eq_one_of_not_dvd.lean

